        '0.12': '"For, judging by your sorrow, your more than human beauty and your ascetic garb, you are surely Rama\'s queen."',
        '0.13': 'Hearing his words, and delighted by the praise of Rama, Vaidehi spoke to Hanuman, who was perched in the tree:',
        '0.14': '"I am the daughter-in-law of Dasharatha, foremost of the lion-like kings on earth, the self-possessed destroyer of enemy armies.',
        '0.15': '"I am the daughter of the great-souled Janaka of Videha; my name is Sita, and I am the wife of the wise Rama.',
        '0.16': '"For twelve years I lived there in Raghava\'s house, enjoying human pleasures, all my desires fulfilled.',
        '0.17': '"Then in the thirteenth year the king, with his preceptors, set about consecrating the delight of the Ikshvakus in the kingdom.',
